# The push gate goes through `scripts/pnpm-invocation.ts` instead of the bare
# name `pnpm`, for the same reason as the commit gate: here the launcher RESOLVES
# and then exits 127, so the bare name turns every push into a hand-built PATH
# shim. No `set -e` here either: husky's shim already runs this file as `sh -e`
# (see `.husky/_/h`), and the resolver exits non-zero on its own, so the build
# gate fails by itself.
#
# `test:affected` is deliberately NOT here. When the scope resolves to the full
# unit tier it declines to run it and exits non-zero, so a push gate built on it
# could decide to gate nothing. CI's one full-suite verdict is `pnpm exec turbo run test --filter=//`.
node scripts/pnpm-invocation.ts run build
